  "coverage": [
    "Stored recovery baselines remain independent of unsaved suffixes and requested revisions in row/blob layouts and mutable/const writes.",
    "Readable loads, last, exports and forks tolerate damaged session tokens without regenerating them; ordinary session mutations reject them before token-rotating SQL.",
    "Token-only repair preserves unreadable raw transcript/provider bytes, provider revisions, journal, references and metadata; valid tokens are no-ops; backup/commit failures and two invalidations preserve original errors.",
    "Completion replaces provenance-identified provisional outcomes, supports retained const recovery and multiple live calls, rejects differing repeated output, and reloads without duplicate results.",
    "An agent-level process executor counter verifies one actual execution with one or two forced publication invalidations.",
    "Original Error subtypes, private revision subtypes, JSON exceptions, provider status/body, cancellation code, allocation failures and non-standard exceptions survive receipt/diagnostic failure.",
    "Missing absolute checkpoint archives, strict cache fallback, receipt eviction, prefix edits, external unknown JSON fields, and mutable handoff after const writes remain covered.",
    "Both same-connection reconciliation invalidations and the restored external-connection/archive-read scenario retain the two-attempt bound.",
    "Allocation interception verifies nonthrowing completion and const-receipt acknowledgement after an owning commit; matching nothrow allocator overloads keep sanitizer allocation pairs consistent."
  ],
